====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
  IF a standard heuristic beats Qiskit's grouper, the saving is free: it is
  seconds of classical preprocessing against circuits saved on EVERY gradient
  for the whole optimisation run. nisq_v6._group would take the best of
  several rather than whatever `group_commuting` returns.

  IF Qiskit already wins or ties, its grouper is doing as well as the standard
  greedy family and the remaining gap to the true MCC optimum is not
  reachable this cheaply - which is itself worth knowing, because it closes
  the question rather than leaving it as a vague 'maybe better heuristics'.

  EITHER WAY THIS IS NOT A NEW METHOD. The MCC formulation and these
  heuristics are arXiv:1907.03358's, from 2019. What is measured here is the
  gap on THIS Hamiltonian family at THESE sizes, which is a sizing result.

  Scope: v30's JW generator, four sizes, coefficients ignored (neither
  grouping depends on them), greedy heuristics only - no exact MCC, no
  simulated annealing, no LP relaxation.
